                  "content": "Chemical bonding is a primary mechanism in molecular chemistry. Atoms form covalent, ionic, and metallic bonds to achieve stable octet configurations. Covalent bonding involves shared electron pairs between atoms, whereas ionic bonding is the complete transfer of valence electrons.",
