                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "rwYUQ",
                  "name": "paragraph",
                  "fill": "#5c564f",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "The SN2 reaction is a bimolecular nucleophilic substitution characterized by a single concerted step. The nucleophile performs a backside attack on the electrophilic carbon, opposite to the leaving group, causing a Walden inversion of stereocenter.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.45,
                  "fontFamily": "Lora",
                  "fontSize": 14,
